  "question": "The Brewsters angle $i_b$ for an interface should be :",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$0° < i_b < 30°$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$30° < i_b < 45°$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$45° < i_b < 90°$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$i_b = 90°$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "C",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "Brewster's law: $\\tan i_b = n$.\n\nFor light going from air into a denser medium, $n > 1$, so $\\tan i_b > 1$. Since $i_b < 90°$,\n$$45° < i_b < 90°$$",
